# client-custom-fields.absent-scope-matrix.must-fail.patch
#
# Targets: AC-37 (the runtime scope surface) — a composable that DECLARES a
# meaningful scope matrix must publish it on the EXPORTED wrapper, so
# `useModulePort.ts`'s `servesActor(composable.scopeMatrix, actor)` — which runs
# BEFORE any call — reads the real cell set, not `undefined`.
#
# Authored by: developer seat (agent-seat-separation.companion.md — the seat
# that knows the exact line it changed authors the mutant; the prover applies
# it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to construct it).
#
# RE-TARGETED (developer seat, FE-3240 second pass): the prior hunk deleted the
# COLLECTION's (`useClientCustomFields.ts`) explicit `.scopeMatrix` assignment.
# FE-3240 removed that assignment BY DESIGN — the collection names NO context
# (all-`never` matrix, client rides in `.withId()`), so it intentionally
# publishes no matrix and `servesActor(undefined)` reads as "serve every actor,
# gate at runtime". AC-37's collection case now tolerates an absent matrix
# (`values(collMatrix ?? {})`), so no collection mutation can flip it. The live
# matrix-presence invariant now lives on the IMAGE editor, which DOES declare a
# meaningful cell (CLIENT->FIELD) and MUST publish it. Same capability under
# test ("a module publishes its declared scope matrix as a value"), moved to the
# composable that still carries one.
#
# Mutates: useClientCustomFieldImage.ts — deletes the explicit
# `(useClientCustomFieldImage as ScopedComposable<...>).scopeMatrix =
# CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELD_IMAGE_SCOPE_MATRIX;` statement. The `@decision` doc block
# immediately above it is left standing — the code no longer does what its own
# doc block says it does, which is the point of the mutation.
#
# Expected RED: client-custom-fields.surface.test.ts —
# "AC-37 the IMAGE editor carries its unchanged CLIENT->FIELD matrix on the
# exported function, before any call" — `useClientCustomFieldImage.scopeMatrix`
# reads `undefined` instead of deep-equal to `CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELD_IMAGE_SCOPE_MATRIX`.
#
# Apply / verify / revert:
#   git apply <this file>
#   pnpm --filter @upmind-automation/headless test client-custom-fields.surface   # must go RED
#   git apply -R <this file>
#
diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/useClientCustomFieldImage.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/useClientCustomFieldImage.ts
index eed065710..ad76cd92c 100644
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/useClientCustomFieldImage.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-custom-fields/useClientCustomFieldImage.ts
@@ -129,13 +129,6 @@ export function useClientCustomFieldImage(): ScopeBuilder<
  *   still `undefined` until the first call, and `useModulePort` reads it
  *   before any call happens.
  */
-(
-  useClientCustomFieldImage as ScopedComposable<
-    ReturnType<typeof createClientCustomFieldImageForScope>,
-    ClientCustomFieldImageScopeMatrix
-  >
-).scopeMatrix = CLIENT_CUSTOM_FIELD_IMAGE_SCOPE_MATRIX;
-
 // Type export for consumers
 export type UseClientCustomFieldImage = ReturnType<
   typeof useClientCustomFieldImage
